# ASAI — data is non-negotiable

ASAI is about **all** data, not only alerts or “aberrant” readings.

- Never remove, disable, thin, sample-down, or skip history/logging/telemetry features to improve WiFi, cost, latency, or convenience without **explicit user approval first**.
- Every device measurement that is published live must also be retained in history (e.g. RTDB `/live` and `/log`) unless the user decides otherwise.
- Prefer fixing reliability around full data (retry, queue, reconnect) over dropping data.
- Do not silently change data retention, publish cadence for the sake of dropping logs, or alert-only architectures.
